# Observability Lab: Distributed Trace Waterfall & Root Span Analysis

## 1. Transaction Overview & Architecture Context

The distributed transaction represents an order-placement request across multiple microservices.

- Request Method: POST
- Request Endpoint: /api/v2/orders
- Client ID: cust_882194
- Trace ID: tr-7b94e18f2c3a50d6
- Root Span ID: span-gw-01
- Total Transaction Duration: 5420 ms
- Total Spans: 8
- Transaction Outcome: HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout
- Timestamp: 2026-11-14T15:10:04.120Z

Services involved in the distributed transaction:

- api-gateway
- order-service
- auth-service
- inventory-service
- pricing-service
- payment-service
- payment-db

The request entered through the API Gateway and was passed to the order-service. The order-service successfully completed authentication, inventory reservation, and pricing operations before calling the payment-service.

The payment-service then called the external payment provider. The external authorization call timed out, causing the payment operation to fail. The failure propagated back through the order-service and API Gateway, resulting in an HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout.

